From 4d2ba64257ef80d1bbcde06f3e1762d9326f0a8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:45:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw: the store does not wait 100 ms under its lock

Why: before writing over a file Core did not write, the store refused
one changed in the last second, and otherwise statted it, slept 100 ms
and statted it again, holding its mutex. Every writer (Config page,
Controls page, IMU calibration, storage switches) waited behind that
sleep. The age check already catches an editor that is saving (nano
rewrites in place, vim and os.replace writers such as the owner's
campaign tool rename in one step), so the second stat only adds a
writer that pauses over a second between two writes. Original
Apertar's whole-file save has no such check at all
(saveHardwareConfigFile, src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp:5323-5386 at
upstream-1.6.0).

What: settledLocked keeps the 1 s age check and returns; the sleep, the
second stat and the <thread> include are gone. The comment says the
lock must not sleep.

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and the 18 host tests pass; the KB
controls_store_test passes (52 of 52, incl. "a fresh hand edit is not
merged into"). --simulate: a file replaced with os.replace just before
a key edit -> being_written; 1.5 s later the edit is written and keeps
the outside line, reply in 12 ms. Pi: none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp | 10 +++-------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
index f7e9dba..77837f9 100644
--- a/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
+++ b/src/hardware/HardwareConfigStore.cpp
@@ -11,7 +11,6 @@
 #include <map>
 #include <memory>
 #include <sstream>
-#include <thread>
 
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 
@@ -205,18 +204,15 @@ std::optional<std::string> HardwareConfigStore::baseTextLocked(const std::string
     return std::nullopt;
 }
 
-// A file Core did not write must not be edited while an editor may still be saving it (nano rewrites in place).
+// A file Core did not write must not be edited while an editor may still be saving it (nano rewrites in place):
+// one changed in the last second is left alone. Never sleep here: every writer waits on mutex_.
 bool HardwareConfigStore::settledLocked() const
 {
     if (!stamp_.exists || revision_ == state_.writtenRevision)
         return true;
     const auto now = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(std::chrono::system_clock::now().time_since_epoch()).count();
     const int64_t age = now - stamp_.mtimeNs;
-    if (age >= 0 && age < 1000000000)
-        return false;
-    const Stamp first = statFile();
-    std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(100));
-    return first == statFile();
+    return !(age >= 0 && age < 1000000000);
 }
 
 std::string HardwareConfigStore::currentText() const
